Package: CompreSSoR
Type: Package
Title: Compressed GWAS Summary Statistics
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Fergus", "Hamilton", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "fh6520@users.noreply.github.com")
Author: Fergus Hamilton [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Fergus Hamilton <fh6520@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Convert genome-wide association study summary statistics into a
    compact, block-indexed Pcodec store with a self-contained GRCh38 variant
    identity key, semantic Z/EAF/SE encoding, and explicit import, liftover,
    allele-harmonisation, decompression, and validation tools. P-values and
    beta are reconstructed on demand; Parquet remains available as an
    interoperability backend.
URL: https://github.com/gushamilton/CompreSSoR
BugReports: https://github.com/gushamilton/CompreSSoR/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    data.table (>= 1.15.0),
    digest,
    jsonlite,
    processx
Suggests:
    arrow (>= 23.0.0),
    dplyr,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    rtracklayer,
    GenomicRanges,
    IRanges
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.10; Python 3.12 recommended) with the
    inst/python/requirements.txt runtime for the default Pcodec backend
NeedsCompilation: yes
